{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809459-couple-of-my-home-brewed-merits-for-my-necropolis","id":809459,"title":"Couple of my home brewed merits for my necropolis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-15T02:51:03-08:00","id":809459,"title":"Couple of my home brewed merits for my necropolis","content":"Hello, I figured to make a couple of merits for my upcoming New York Vampire game, and I thought I'd love to get some input on them.<br /> <br /> It's on Tumblr and posted bellow: <a href=\"http://cofdarkness.tumblr.com/post/137340272322/child-of-the-necropolis\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdarkness.tumblr.com/post/1...the-necropolis</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Post copy pasted here: <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">So I figured to make a merit out of the whole Necropolis thing in New York. Still thinking how it should look like\u2026 thoughts? This is oriented and planned for my New York city population, but I try to write it in a more generic form. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Mostly, I\u2019m unsure about naming and general wording\u2026 ideas?</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Pathways of the Necropolis</span> (\u25cf)<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Prerequisites:</span> Status (Nosferatu) (\u25cf) OR Allies(Nosferatu) (\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf)<br /> The character is shown the markings used for the navigation of the Necropolis and now can use it for both city Navigation and getting to it. Most humans will not follow or will be driven away <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Effect:</span><br /> 1. In chases, when the character is trying to escape into the Necropolis, reduce his target number of Successes by 2. <br /> 2. Double his speed for the purposes of traveling around the city on foot, if he uses the Necropolis. </span><br /> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Now, as I mentioned in the last post about #necropolis there\u2019s Revenants in jars there, so the second merit is exactly about that</span><br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Monsters in the Jars </span>(\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Prerequisites: Pathways of the Necropolis (\u25cf), Nightmare (\u25cf), Status (Nosferatu) (\u25cf\u25cf) or Allies(Nosferatu) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The character is shown how to locate and open the Jars containing the Revenants. He\u2019s also taught what kind of illusions and horrors they\u2019ve been trained to follow<br /> He can return them back to life with his Vitae and then using Nightmare cause the appropriate illusions to give them commands. They are terrified and will act out them the most, however they are not able to do menial tasks unless fed first. <br /> When in the Necropolis, roll Wits + Investigation:<br /> <b>Dramatical Failure: </b>You raise a Revenant, but it frenzies and attacks you.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>You fail to find a Revenant<br /> <b>Success: </b>You find a Jar with a Revenant and can return it to life on your next turn by feeding him a point of Vitae<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>You find a Jar with a Revenant and make it fast enough to wake him this turn. </span><br /> <br /> </div> </span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:39:20-08:00","id":810417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809459-couple-of-my-home-brewed-merits-for-my-necropolis#post809459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I figured to make a couple of merits for my upcoming New York Vampire game, and I thought I'd love to get some input on them.<br /> <br /> It's on Tumblr and posted bellow: <a href=\"http://cofdarkness.tumblr.com/post/137340272322/child-of-the-necropolis\" target=\"_blank\">http://cofdarkness.tumblr.com/post/1...the-necropolis</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Post copy pasted here: <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">So I figured to make a merit out of the whole Necropolis thing in New York. Still thinking how it should look like\u2026 thoughts? This is oriented and planned for my New York city population, but I try to write it in a more generic form. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Mostly, I\u2019m unsure about naming and general wording\u2026 ideas?</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Pathways of the Necropolis</span> (\u25cf)<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Prerequisites:</span> Status (Nosferatu) (\u25cf) OR Allies(Nosferatu) (\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf)<br /> The character is shown the markings used for the navigation of the Necropolis and now can use it for both city Navigation and getting to it. Most humans will not follow or will be driven away<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Effect:</span><br /> 1. In chases, when the character is trying to escape into the Necropolis, reduce his target number of Successes by 2.<br /> 2. Double his speed for the purposes of traveling around the city on foot, if he uses the Necropolis. </span><br /> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Now, as I mentioned in the last post about #necropolis there\u2019s Revenants in jars there, so the second merit is exactly about that</span><br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Monsters in the Jars </span>(\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Prerequisites: Pathways of the Necropolis (\u25cf), Nightmare (\u25cf), Status (Nosferatu) (\u25cf\u25cf) or Allies(Nosferatu) (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The character is shown how to locate and open the Jars containing the Revenants. He\u2019s also taught what kind of illusions and horrors they\u2019ve been trained to follow<br /> He can return them back to life with his Vitae and then using Nightmare cause the appropriate illusions to give them commands. They are terrified and will act out them the most, however they are not able to do menial tasks unless fed first.<br /> When in the Necropolis, roll Wits + Investigation:<br /> <b>Dramatical Failure: </b>You raise a Revenant, but it frenzies and attacks you.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>You fail to find a Revenant<br /> <b>Success: </b>You find a Jar with a Revenant and can return it to life on your next turn by feeding him a point of Vitae<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>You find a Jar with a Revenant and make it fast enough to wake him this turn. </span><br /> <br /> </div></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting concepts But would not the larvae fit better thematically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T01:44:16-08:00","id":810536,"title":"","content":"I don't really remember Larvae... And I didn't really care to look up something more fitting when I have something convenient by hand.. + Revenants add to the horror of.. well, them being more common. If Larvae is made.. it's made, in city if you mess up and get a revenant, well, you might want to put him own, or fdo something and here come the Nosferatu to claim him. And if you know what happens to the revenants (Driven insane, scarred beyond any redemption and put in a jar...) you just might be horrified. <br /> <br /> So the whole thing is not just to get servants for the Nosferatu, it's also to put in some &quot;oh shit their monsters&quot; from others. <br /> <br /> Anyways, care to remind me what Larvae are? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T01:47:59-08:00","id":810537,"title":"","content":"They're people whose Embrace immediately forced them into draugr-like mindlessness. They're feral and dangerous, and the artwork has one Kindred literally leading them around on leashes to get the point across. They're like a variant on the Revenant, just instead of being a regular person, they're Humanity 0 and they can be brought back to lucidity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T02:10:10-08:00","id":810543,"title":"","content":"While it's cool, I like the image of Nosferatu taking perfectly fine Revenants from the city (well, fine compared to a larvae). Anyways, thanks for the suggestion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:34:24-08:00","id":812126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809459-couple-of-my-home-brewed-merits-for-my-necropolis?p=810536#post810536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really remember Larvae... And I didn't really care to look up something more fitting when I have something convenient by hand.. + Revenants add to the horror of.. well, them being more common. If Larvae is made.. it's made, in city if you mess up and get a revenant, well, you might want to put him own, or fdo something and here come the Nosferatu to claim him. And if you know what happens to the revenants (Driven insane, scarred beyond any redemption and put in a jar...) you just might be horrified.<br /> <br /> So the whole thing is not just to get servants for the Nosferatu, it's also to put in some &quot;oh shit their monsters&quot; from others.<br /> <br /> Anyways, care to remind me what Larvae are? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well the term was used in Requiem for Rome for something else.<br /> But I'm referring to feral failed embraces from the Wicked Dead. Think pack like kindred version of zombies. There were different ways to control them.<br /> A good film version is that thing from blade that was a product of a failed embrace at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}